thubusercontent.com/u/3395130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc","html_url":"https://github.com/darksylinc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/darksylinc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-09T16:20:57Z","updated_at":"2026-09-09T16:22:00Z","body":"OK I see what happened. **The PR is right and should be merged**.\r\n\r\nI will provide a full timeline of what I recall happened (at least to the best of my memory):\r\n\r\n- TheForge added Swappy, but it just added the library and turned it on with defaults\r\n- I had done research on Swappy and designed this [3-setting enum on OgreNext](https://github.com/OGRECave/ogre-next/blob/475f783d76f21b530e718aab4a548cdd9a222e50/RenderSystems/Vulkan/src/Windowing/Android/OgreVulkanAndroidWindow.cpp#L289-L304) (link to [enum header](https://github.com/OGRECave/ogre-next/blob/475f783d76f21b530e718aab4a548cdd9a222e50/RenderSystems/Vulkan/include/Windowing/Android/OgreVulkanAndroidWindow.h#L73-L103)). If you look at the code, OgreNext's settings are correct (as it would be post-PR)\r\n- If you notice carefully, the switch statement has `PipelineForcedOn`/`PIPELINE_FORCED_ON` and `AutoVSyncInterval_AutoPipeline`/`AUTO_FPS_AUTO_PIPELINE` case labels flipped, but not their body statements. It may have to do with with Godot coding practices, or our discussions about what the default argument should be.\r\n\r\nRegarding the default argument: I remember the discussion was:\r\n\r\n1. **Keep backwards compatibility / same behavior:** This would mean defaulting to `PIPELINE_FORCED_ON` (if using correct semantics).\r\n2. **Keep same behavior as PC:** This would mean defaulting to `PIPELINE_FORCED_ON` (if using correct semantics).\r\n3. **Provide the best experience for Android out of the box:** There is no single definition of what's \"best\", because it involves smoothness, input latency, performance and battery consumption. Nonetheless there is a massive framerate stabilization when selecting either `AUTO_FPS_PIPELINE_FORCED_ON` or `AUTO_FPS_AUTO_PIPELINE`, causing a much smoother experience, therefore one of those should be the default. I think we agreed on this one becoming the default (that's what the documentation says) because of its impact on the overall experience.\r\n\r\nTL;DR: The PR is right. The logic sequence is flipped.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5605130364/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5607912779","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123300#issuecomment-5607912779","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123300","id":5607912779,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABTkH1Sw","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Re